# Context

Copy this to `context.md` and fill it in — or point `CONTEXT_MD_PATH` in your
`.env` at an already-filled copy (e.g. `generic-lab/context.md`, if you built
that first) so you're not maintaining the same document twice.

This is read on every single judge call. It's the "who Arjun is" the bot
uses to decide LIKE/SKIP and to write in your voice. Same file, same rules,
as generic-lab — see that project's `context.md` for the full template if you
want the long-form version. Short version below.

---

## Basics
- **Age:**
- **City:**

## What you're looking for
_Specific, not "something serious."_

## Who you're trying to attract
_Describe her, not a checklist of traits._

## Your actual life
_Specific things you do. This is the raw material for openers — the model
can only reference what's here._

## Your voice
_Paste 3-4 real messages you've sent friends, uncleaned. Used alongside the
sent-message voice bank the bot builds automatically over time._

## Constraints
_Anything off the table._
